.TH tkuhexedit n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkuhexedit
.SS Name
.PP
\fBtkutils::tkuhexedit\fR \- small Tcl/Tk hex viewer/editor widget.
.SS Synopsis
.CS
package require tkutils::tkuhexedit

set w [::tkutils::tkuhexedit::widget .hex]
pack $w -fill both -expand 1

::tkutils::tkuhexedit::loadFile $w file.bin
::tkutils::tkuhexedit::gotoOffset $w 0x100
::tkutils::tkuhexedit::findHex $w {50 4B 03 04}
::tkutils::tkuhexedit::patchHex $w 0x100 {00 FF}
::tkutils::tkuhexedit::saveFile $w
.CE
.SS Description
.PP
The widget displays binary data as offset, hexadecimal bytes and printable ASCII. It provides a compact GUI for inspection and small length\-preserving patches.
.PP
\fBpatchHex\fR replaces existing bytes. It does not insert or delete bytes.
.SS "Public procedures"
.CS
widget path ?options?
loadFile path filename
saveFile path ?filename?
setData path bytes
getData path
gotoOffset path offset
findText path pattern ?start?
findHex path hex ?start?
patchHex path offset hex
render path ?offset?
.CE
.SS "Options for widget"
.CS
-width        text widget width
-height       text widget height
-bytesperline bytes per rendered line, default 16
.CE
.SS Limits
.IP \(bu
Not a full binary editor.
.IP \(bu
No insert/delete mode.
.IP \(bu
No large\-file streaming yet; data is kept in memory.
.IP \(bu
Requires Tk and therefore a graphical display.
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtclutils::tubin\fR, \fBtclutils::tuhexdump\fR, \fBtclutils::common\fR (required).
